  "status_text": "Checked in Lean, from an outside contributor: once one copy of a symmetric bipartite graph with n vertices a side is paid for, each further copy, up to 2^k in all, takes at most 4n more AND/OR gates of fan-in at most two to represent, however costly that one copy was [L-meta-18672]. It says nothing about what one copy costs. On the crown, a solver's run at five a side ended undecided (computed), its control too, so it shows nothing either way; the statement that every cheapest crown circuit reads each input exactly once stays open [L-meta-18664].",
